{"type":"data","nodes":[null,null,{"type":"data","data":[{"species":1,"photos":211,"maps":438},[2,15,27,39,50,62,74,85,95,107,119,131,142,154,166,177,189,200],{"id":3,"scientificName":4,"inaturalistTaxon":4,"names":5,"hint":8,"hintSource":11,"preservedInCaptivity":14},"bison","Bison bison",{"fr":6,"en":7},"Bison d'Amérique","American bison",{"fr":9,"en":10},"Le plus grand mammifère terrestre d'Amérique du Nord. Avant l'arrivée des colons européens, 50 à 70 millions de bisons vivaient du Mexique au Canada.","Endemic to North America, the American bison once roamed a vast grassland belt stretching from Alaska to the Gulf of Mexico.",{"fr":12,"en":13},"https://fr.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bison_d%27Am%C3%A9rique","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/American_bison",false,{"id":16,"scientificName":17,"inaturalistTaxon":17,"names":18,"hint":21,"hintSource":24,"preservedInCaptivity":14},"flamant-rose","Phoenicopterus roseus",{"fr":19,"en":20},"Flamant rose","Greater flamingo",{"fr":22,"en":23},"Le flamant le plus répandu : on le trouve dans certaines parties de l'Afrique, de l'Asie et du sud de l'Europe.","The most widespread flamingo, found in Africa, the Indian subcontinent, the Middle East and Mediterranean Europe.",{"fr":25,"en":26},"https://fr.wikipedia.org/wiki/Flamant_rose","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Greater_flamingo",{"id":28,"scientificName":29,"inaturalistTaxon":29,"names":30,"hint":33,"hintSource":36,"preservedInCaptivity":14},"girafe","Giraffa",{"fr":31,"en":32},"Girafe","Giraffe",{"fr":34,"en":35},"Les girafes vivent dans les savanes africaines, du Tchad jusqu'en Afrique du Sud.","The tallest living land animal, the giraffe is a large hoofed mammal of Africa.",{"fr":37,"en":38},"https://fr.wikipedia.org/wiki/Girafe","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Giraffe",{"id":40,"scientificName":41,"inaturalistTaxon":41,"names":42,"hint":44,"hintSource":47,"preservedInCaptivity":14},"gorille","Gorilla",{"fr":43,"en":41},"Gorille",{"fr":45,"en":46},"Les gorilles vivent en groupes dans les forêts tropicales d'Afrique ; ceux des montagnes habitent les forêts des monts Virunga.","Gorillas are great apes that live in the tropical forests of equatorial Africa.",{"fr":48,"en":49},"https://fr.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gorille","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gorilla",{"id":51,"scientificName":52,"inaturalistTaxon":52,"names":53,"hint":56,"hintSource":59,"preservedInCaptivity":14},"herisson","Erinaceus europaeus",{"fr":54,"en":55},"Hérisson d'Europe","European hedgehog",{"fr":57,"en":58},"Le hérisson d'Europe est répandu dans toute l'Europe, sauf le grand Nord, ainsi qu'en Turquie et dans le Caucase.","Native to Europe, from Iberia and Italy north to Scandinavia and west to Ireland.",{"fr":60,"en":61},"https://fr.wikipedia.org/wiki/Erinaceus_europaeus","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/European_hedgehog",{"id":63,"scientificName":64,"inaturalistTaxon":64,"names":65,"hint":68,"hintSource":71,"preservedInCaptivity":14},"kangourou-roux","Osphranter rufus",{"fr":66,"en":67},"Kangourou roux","Red kangaroo",{"fr":69,"en":70},"Le plus grand marsupial vivant parcourt presque toute l'Australie, sauf les zones les plus fertiles du sud, de la côte est et des forêts tropicales du nord.","The largest living marsupial roams mainland Australia, except its more fertile areas: the south-west, the eastern coasts and the northern rainforests.",{"fr":72,"en":73},"https://fr.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kangourou_roux","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Red_kangaroo",{"id":75,"scientificName":76,"inaturalistTaxon":76,"names":77,"hint":79,"hintSource":82,"preservedInCaptivity":14},"koala","Phascolarctos cinereus",{"fr":78,"en":78},"Koala",{"fr":80,"en":81},"Endémique d'Australie, le koala vit dans les régions côtières de l'est et du sud, d'Adélaïde au sud de la péninsule du cap York.","Native to Australia, the koala lives in coastal areas of the continent's eastern and southern regions.",{"fr":83,"en":84},"https://fr.wikipedia.org/wiki/Koala","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Koala",{"id":86,"scientificName":87,"inaturalistTaxon":87,"names":88,"hint":90,"hintSource":93,"preservedInCaptivity":14},"lion","Panthera leo",{"fr":89,"en":89},"Lion",{"fr":91,"en":92},"Le lion ne vit plus qu'en Afrique subsaharienne et en Inde.","The lion now ranges only in Sub-Saharan Africa and India.",{"fr":94,"en":94},"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lion",{"id":96,"scientificName":97,"inaturalistTaxon":97,"names":98,"hint":101,"hintSource":104,"preservedInCaptivity":14},"loup-gris","Canis lupus",{"fr":99,"en":100},"Loup gris","Grey wolf",{"fr":102,"en":103},"Le loup gris est largement réparti en Eurasie et en Amérique du Nord.","The grey wolf is native to Eurasia and North America.",{"fr":105,"en":106},"https://fr.wikipedia.org/wiki/Canis_lupus","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wolf",{"id":108,"scientificName":109,"inaturalistTaxon":109,"names":110,"hint":113,"hintSource":116,"preservedInCaptivity":14},"manchot-empereur","Aptenodytes forsteri",{"fr":111,"en":112},"Manchot empereur","Emperor penguin",{"fr":114,"en":115},"Le plus grand et le plus lourd des manchots est endémique de l'Antarctique.","The tallest and heaviest of all penguins is endemic to Antarctica.",{"fr":117,"en":118},"https://fr.wikipedia.org/wiki/Manchot_empereur","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Emperor_penguin",{"id":120,"scientificName":121,"inaturalistTaxon":121,"names":122,"hint":125,"hintSource":128,"preservedInCaptivity":14},"orang-outan","Pongo",{"fr":123,"en":124},"Orang-outan","Orangutan",{"fr":126,"en":127},"Les orangs-outans ne vivent que dans les forêts tropicales de Sumatra et de Bornéo, partagées entre l'Indonésie et la Malaisie.","Orangutans now live only in parts of Borneo and Sumatra, though they once ranged across Southeast Asia and South China.",{"fr":129,"en":130},"https://fr.wikipedia.org/wiki/Orang-outan","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Orangutan",{"id":132,"scientificName":133,"inaturalistTaxon":133,"names":134,"hint":137,"hintSource":140,"preservedInCaptivity":14},"ours-blanc","Ursus maritimus",{"fr":135,"en":136},"Ours blanc","Polar bear",{"fr":138,"en":139},"L'ours blanc vit dans l'Arctique et les régions voisines ; ses larges pattes lui permettent de marcher sur la glace.","The polar bear lives in the Arctic and nearby areas; its large paws let it walk on ice.",{"fr":141,"en":141},"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Polar_bear",{"id":143,"scientificName":144,"inaturalistTaxon":144,"names":145,"hint":148,"hintSource":151,"preservedInCaptivity":14},"panda","Ailuropoda melanoleuca",{"fr":146,"en":147},"Panda géant","Giant panda",{"fr":149,"en":150},"Le panda géant est endémique de Chine : il ne vit nulle part ailleurs à l'état sauvage.","Endemic to China, the giant panda feeds almost entirely on bamboo.",{"fr":152,"en":153},"https://fr.wikipedia.org/wiki/Panda_g%C3%A9ant","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Giant_panda",{"id":155,"scientificName":156,"inaturalistTaxon":156,"names":157,"hint":160,"hintSource":163,"preservedInCaptivity":14},"paresseux","Bradypus",{"fr":158,"en":159},"Paresseux à trois doigts","Three-toed sloth",{"fr":161,"en":162},"Les paresseux à trois doigts vivent dans les arbres, en Amérique du Sud et en Amérique centrale.","Three-toed sloths are tree-dwelling mammals of the American tropics.",{"fr":164,"en":165},"https://fr.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bradypus","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Three-toed_sloth",{"id":167,"scientificName":168,"inaturalistTaxon":168,"names":169,"hint":172,"hintSource":175,"preservedInCaptivity":14},"pygargue","Haliaeetus leucocephalus",{"fr":170,"en":171},"Pygargue à tête blanche","Bald eagle",{"fr":173,"en":174},"Ce rapace d'Amérique du Nord vit près des grandes étendues d'eau, de l'Alaska et du Canada jusqu'au nord du Mexique.","A sea eagle of North America, found near large bodies of open water from Alaska and Canada to northern Mexico.",{"fr":176,"en":176},"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bald_eagle",{"id":178,"scientificName":179,"inaturalistTaxon":179,"names":180,"hint":183,"hintSource":186,"preservedInCaptivity":14},"renne","Rangifer tarandus",{"fr":181,"en":182},"Renne (caribou)","Reindeer (caribou)",{"fr":184,"en":185},"Appelé caribou en Amérique du Nord, le renne vit dans les régions arctiques et subarctiques d'Europe, d'Asie et d'Amérique du Nord.","Called caribou in North America, the reindeer lives all around the Arctic: tundra and boreal forests of Northern Europe, Siberia and North America.",{"fr":187,"en":188},"https://fr.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rangifer_tarandus","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Reindeer",{"id":190,"scientificName":191,"inaturalistTaxon":191,"names":192,"hint":195,"hintSource":198,"preservedInCaptivity":14},"tigre","Panthera tigris",{"fr":193,"en":194},"Tigre","Tiger",{"fr":196,"en":197},"Grand félin au pelage orange rayé de noir, le tigre est originaire d'Asie.","A large cat with orange fur and black stripes, the tiger is native to Asia.",{"fr":199,"en":199},"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tiger",{"id":201,"scientificName":202,"inaturalistTaxon":202,"names":203,"hint":206,"hintSource":209,"preservedInCaptivity":14},"zebre","Equus quagga",{"fr":204,"en":205},"Zèbre des plaines","Plains zebra",{"fr":207,"en":208},"Le zèbre le plus répandu : son aire, morcelée, couvre une grande partie de l'Afrique australe et orientale, au sud du Sahara.","The most widespread zebra: its fragmented range spans much of southern and eastern Africa, south of the Sahara.",{"fr":210,"en":210},"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Plains_zebra",[212,220,226,231,234,237,241,246,252,256,260,265,270,275,278,281,285,289,293,296,301,305,309,313,317,321,325,329,333,338,342,347,351,355,359,363,367,371,375,379,385,388,392,396,401,406,410,414,418,422,426,430,434],{"speciesId":28,"file":213,"width":214,"height":215,"attribution":216,"license":217,"sourceUrl":218,"modifications":219},"images/photos/19df4e4a9b82ee54.webp",1024,768,"no rights reserved","cc0","https://www.inaturalist.org/photos/12238621","Redimensionnée (1 024 px au plus) et convertie en WebP ; métadonnées retirées.",{"speciesId":28,"file":221,